BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What did Tanyka eat? Reconstructing the diet of an ancient Brazili
 an tetra…
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260911T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260911T130000
DTSTAMP:20260829T134008Z
UID:ff295f582d4665ed8d4416b5f2028823@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: STEM\\n\\nSee an ‘ancient living fossil
 ’ and hear about the research into their diet being led by Syd Joheim\, 
 Prince Intern\, and Ken Angielczyk\, MacArthur Curator of Paleomammalogy. 
 Tanyka\, a Permian stem tetrapod from Brazil\, is known only for its jaws 
 that have extensive fields of tiny teeth on their inner surface. These un
 ique features suggest they had a different diet than other early tetrapod
 s who lived over 275 million years ago. Discover how researchers hope to g
 ain insight into what it might have been eating by comparing the complexi
 ty of these teeth to those of other contemporary species and examining mi
 cro-wear patterns on the teeth to reconstruct their diet.\\n\\nMore info: 
 https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/what-did-tanyka-ea
 t-reconstructing-the-diet-of-an-ancient-brazilian-tetrapod
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/what-did-tanyk
 a-eat-reconstructing-the-diet-of-an-ancient-brazilian-tetrapod
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: What did Tanyka eat? Reconstructing the diet of an a
 ncient B
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: What did Tanyka eat? Reconstructing the diet of an
  ancient B
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
